%N A395921 Decimal expansion of Sum_{n>=0} (-1)^n*eta^(n)(n)/n!, where eta^(n) denotes the n-th derivative of the Dirichlet eta function.
%H A395921 Jwalin Bhatt, <a href="/A395921/b395921.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A395921 Marvin Ray Burns, <a href="https://forums.wolfram.com/mathgroup/archive/2013/Mar/msg00057.html">Regularized sums involving the MRB constant</a>, Wolfram MathGroup post, Mar 2013.
%H A395921 OEIS Wiki, <a href="/wiki/MRB_constant">MRB constant</a>.
%H A395921 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/MRBConstant.html">MRB Constant</a>.
%F A395921 Equals 1/2 - A037077.
%F A395921 Equals -Sum_{n>=1} (-1)^n*n^(1/n).
%e A395921 0.31214035753793287975148206594572676994409690509986121382799...
%t A395921 N[Sum[(-1)^k/k! Limit[D[DirichletEta[s], {s, k}], s -> k], {k, 0, 50}], 20]
%t A395921 (* Alternative: *)
%t A395921 1/2 - NSum[(-1)^n*(n^(1/n) - 1), {n, 1, Infinity}, WorkingPrecision -> 30, Method -> "AlternatingSigns"]
%o A395921 (PARI) 1/2 - sumalt(n=1, (-1)^n*(n^(1/n) - 1))
